00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:21.149
level to justify our usefulness over a robot.
So what are you finding in your research?

00:21:21.149 --> 00:21:25.700
What are the consequences of multitasking
or our continuous partial attention?

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:30.419
Yeah. I haven't studied multitasking in particular.
Most of the stuff I've looked at it's more

00:21:30.419 --> 00:21:34.749
in the social domain as opposed to the cognitive,
although the really interesting thing about

00:21:34.749 --> 00:21:40.660
smartphones is now you're multitasking with
social information as well. And with multitasking

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:45.919
it sort of does depend on the kind of multitasking.
So if you are task switching very rapidly

00:21:45.919 --> 00:21:51.240
in certain cases, you're not actually able
to multitask what we think of as holding two

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:56.200
things in your mind. You're going back and
forth and so as you mentioned there are some

00:21:56.200 --> 00:22:00.759
disadvantages to doing that. On the other
hand there are certain ways that if you're

00:22:00.759 --> 00:22:04.830
multitasking during a video game, if you're
playing sort of an action video game where

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:09.519
you have a lot of information in the environment
and you have to keep track of that first person

00:22:09.519 --> 00:22:13.420
shooter, for example, those are situations
where you might have someone over here and

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:17.740
over there and now you are multitasking in
the sense that your attention is focused in

00:22:17.740 --> 00:22:18.820
multiple areas.

00:22:18.820 --> 00:22:23.029
And the really interesting thing is that there's
some research that finds that those kind of

00:22:23.029 --> 00:22:30.309
games do improve your ability to hold information
in your mind at once. And so when we say multitasking

00:22:30.309 --> 00:22:34.559
it really depends on what we're talking about
because on the one hand you get people who

00:22:34.559 --> 00:22:39.230
are gamers are actually better at one kind
of multitasking. On the other hand people

00:22:39.230 --> 00:22:43.019
who tend to report that they do a lot of using
social media while they're doing homework

00:22:43.019 --> 00:22:49.080
and that sort of thing that they often will
show lower performance on certain tasks. So

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:53.940
again it's this idea that it really depends
on how you define it, that there are these

00:22:53.940 --> 00:22:59.110
benefits or detriments but it's not one thing
even with multitasking.

00:22:59.110 --> 00:23:05.169
Interestingly when you survey, surveys were
done a couple of years ago and you ask high

00:23:05.169 --> 00:23:09.220
