think that your performance academically,

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:13.399
when you're sitting doing your homework is
degraded?” they'll say no no no!

00:23:13.399 --> 00:23:14.639
Yeah.

00:23:14.639 --> 00:23:21.480
I think, unless someone here knows more, it's
really only the first person shooter action

00:23:21.480 --> 00:23:27.080
video games that is suggesting that you can
get good at that kind of multitasking. So

00:23:27.080 --> 00:23:30.889
you're entirely right you have to think about
what do we mean by multitasking.

00:23:30.889 --> 00:23:31.889
If you're playing….

00:23:31.889 --> 00:23:37.160
Wait, are you saying that if I let my son
play first the first person shooter video

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:40.909
games then he'll be able to listen to music
and

00:23:40.909 --> 00:23:41.909
No,then he’ll be able to..

00:23:41.909 --> 00:23:42.909
Watch instagram while he's doing his homework?

00:23:42.909 --> 00:23:47.409
I wouldn't count on it. Then he'll be able
to do the first person shooter games really

00:23:47.409 --> 00:23:54.760
well. And we really don't know about transferability
to other domains. We know there's certain

00:23:54.760 --> 00:24:00.110
kinds of activities that go together. If you
play the piano you need two hands and you

00:24:00.110 --> 00:24:05.039
need your feet. OK, is that multitasking?
It is in the version because all you have

00:24:05.039 --> 00:24:09.630
to do is look at someone learning to play
the piano to begin with. And you can't coordinate

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:14.679
both hands. I'll never forget when I was teaching
my son to drive, he said I'll look ahead and

00:24:14.679 --> 00:24:20.889
you look in the mirrors for me because I can't
do both. And then eventually you'll learn

00:24:20.889 --> 00:24:23.590
you have to coordinate those pieces.

00:24:23.590 --> 00:24:27.940
There has been research that suggests there
are certain people, maybe two to five percent

00:24:27.940 --> 00:24:33.429
of the population who are super taskers who
actually can do well in multitasking. But

00:24:33.429 --> 00:24:36.860
the experiments that were done at Stanford
a number of years ago said the people who

00:24:36.860 --> 00:24:42.869
say I'm really good at multitasking were probably
worse. In fact the data shed showed were worse

00:24:42.869 --> 00:24:47.049
than the people so I'm sorry I can't keep
track of multiple things at the same time.

00:24:47.049 --> 00:24:50.899
But there's one other point I'd like to make
if I could and that has to do with what is

00:24:50.899 --> 00:24:58.019
it we mean by learning? And part of the question
about whether digital technologies are helping

00:24:58.019 --> 00:25:04.610
us learn or not is that on the one hand digital
technologies are really good for finding facts.

00:25:04.610 --> 00:25:09.940
Or for finding pieces of information which
may be collections of facts. And we use the

00:25:09.940 --> 00:25:18.749
technologies for getting those little pieces.
However if we don't have a context that says

00:25:18.749 --> 00:25:23.040
there is more to learning than this…there's
is something we want to call knowledge. There's

00:25:23.040 --> 00:25:28.240
something that's called two years from now.
How did you integrate those pieces that you

00:25:28.240 --> 00:25:33.929
learned? Then I think we're missing out an
important part of what learning should be

00:25:33.929 --> 00:25:34.929
about.

00:25:34.929 --> 00:25:39.570
The same thing I think goes for adaptive learning
for certain subjects can be absolutely superb

00:25:39.570 --> 00:25:45.169
and far better than the vast majority of teachers
most of us have had. On the other hand one

00:25:45.169 --> 00:25:50.820
of the problems or one of the challenges of
adaptive learning is if we say this could

00:25:50.820 --> 00:25:59.690
work in any discipline, you then have to say
for doing philosophy how do you make that

00:25:59.690 --> 00:26:04.419
adaptive for a learning tool. And are those
the things that are most important to learn

00:26:04.419 --> 00:26:09.919
in philosophy or is that a way of thinking
about problems? And I don't know that we know

00:26:09.919 --> 00:26:14.649
how to code that into smaller pieces and if
you can figure it out please help.

00:26:14.649 --> 00:26:21.769
I'm not sure that's something that I can figure
out this moment but I can say that the term

00:26:21.769 --> 00:26:26.440
‘adaptive learning’ evokes certain people
and certain ideas in certain people and from

00:26:26.440 --> 00:26:32.799
just just listening to how you describe it
I can imagine how you would think about it

00:26:32.799 --> 00:26:36.990
and I imagine everybody else here has a different
opportunity, a different experience and what

00:26:36.990 --> 00:26:41.259
adaptive might have meant. And that's the
problem with adaptivity and personalization

00:26:41.259 --> 00:26:45.070
as this other buzzword that we're using right
now personalized learning, adaptive learning,

00:26:45.070 --> 00:26:49.380
individualized learning. And nobody really
knows what the differences are, or better

00:26:49.380 --> 00:26:53.769
yet everybody has their own definition but
uses those words interchangeably.

00:26:53.769 --> 00:26:58.340
So adaptivity the way I would describe it
means that any learner at any time gets what

00:26:58.340 --> 00:27:02.850
that learner needs to succeed. Right? And
if that is applied to philosophy that would

00:27:02.850 --> 00:27:07.159
mean entirely different things than if I learn
math or language. Right but we don't know

00:27:07.159 --> 00:27:12.340
how to do that yet, right? So we have and
I developed just to explain it to myself,

00:27:12.340 --> 00:27:16.840
I developed this taxonomy which is in a new
kind of categories of how one could do adaptive

00:27:16.840 --> 00:27:20.830
learning. And when you look at that entire
taxonomy there are maybe thirty different

00:27:20.830 --> 00:27:24.220
ways of doing that alone on the cognitive
domain but then we have the affective of domain.

00:27:24.220 --> 00:27:29.919
We have a social, cultural domain. We have
have motivational domains of where where we

00:27:29.919 --> 00:27:35.019
could adapt that way. Right. And so when you
look at that and when you look at the existing

00:27:35.019 --> 00:27:39.369
adaptive systems when we're talking about
intelligent tutoring systems and other systems

00:27:39.369 --> 00:27:45.320
that kind of try to guess, to predict what
you need and mostly that means you just solve

00:27:45.320 --> 00:27:50.360
this problem, this math equation. You're not
ready to solve this math equation. It's a

00:27:50.360 --> 00:27:53.710
little harder. Right. That would never work
in philosophy but that's just such a small

00:27:53.710 --> 00:27:59.010
part of what adaptivity could mean. But as
as researchers, as learning scientists we're

00:27:59.010 --> 00:28:01.730
just in the beginning of understanding that.
Or understanding how to build it. We understand

00:28:01.730 --> 00:28:05.250
what we would love to happen but not how to
do it.

00:28:05.250 --> 00:28:10.070
Also if I may, I think we’re in the process
also understanding what it does mean to be

00:28:10.070 --> 00:28:15.650
multitasking because you know the definition
is probably not clear enough. What's often

00:28:15.650 --> 00:28:20.690
described as multitasking is really switching
from one activity to another. There are some

00:28:20.690 --> 00:28:27.870
benefits for multitasking that have been documented
in work with kids, in other persons for example.

00:28:27.870 --> 00:28:32.029
A colleague of mine did some work a good number
